'''Kasli the Bane''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] event. She was added in [[Version 9.5 Update|Version 9.5]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 543
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Kasli the Bane
|name2 = Kasli, Daughter of Chaos
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Kasli, Daughter of Chaos''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Kasli the Bane is a very powerful unit when it comes to stats. The combination of high health and 5 knockbacks leads to her staying alive for a long time when summoned. Thanks to the powerful Surge, she is also able to deliver high and consistent damage to midrangers and backliners, such as [[Le'noir]] and [[R.Ost]], while also intercepting incoming peons and keeping enemies that are extremely easy to knockback at bay, such as Gory variants, [[Brollow]], [[Rain D.]] and [[Mr. Puffington]]. With the Surge from her attack, Kasli can deal up to 11724 DPS at level 30, an incredibly high number. The surge from her attack can destroy smaller peons with ease, allowing powerful, single-target attackers like [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]] and [[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]] to land their hits properly on the main target. This gives Kasli great synergy with them, boosting her value. More likely than not, Kasli can survive long enough for a second Kasli to be deployed, overrunning the stage with pure damage. You can also use her blindspot to stack her on peons before triggering the base, completely destroying the boss and all its support. Lastly, she can even be used for "base trapping": if you have her hit a base and trigger a boss wave, her Surge will instantly hit and severely cripple anything that comes out, sometimes making a massive difference. This is also especially effective on certain [[Ranking Dojo|Catclaw Dojo]] challenges as the surge itself can hit the base. Just remember that due to her [[Hitbox#Subdivisions|blindspot]] and most of her damage being concentrated in the surge, she will not perform too well against [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]], short ranged pushers like [[Bore]] or [[One Horn]], as well as surge-immune enemies like [[Wild Doge]]. Enemies with [[Surge Attack#Counter-Surge|Counter-Surge]], such as [[Techn-Old Hyena]], are also problematic, as they can abuse her Surge Attacks to flood with their own, destroying anything that isn't Immune. However, a tanky unit can cover her blind spot, making her usage more viable, as are Surge Immune units.

Damage isn't all she has though: her Curse ability lets her disable enemies' Knockback, Slow, Freeze, Weaken, Warp, Curse, Dodge Attack, Toxic, and Drain abilities. Since it has good uptime, this makes her even more useful against enemies with annoying abilities like [[Super Metal Hippoe]], [[Li'l Doge]], [[Crazed Axe Cat (Enemy)|Crazed Axe Cat]], [[Henry]], [[Winged Pigge]], [[Gobble]], [[Heavenly Herald Papuu]], [[Bakoo]] and many [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]]. It also further boosts her synergy by creating openings for attackers that normally would not be able to get past the negative effects, allowing them to reach the target and dish out their payload. There are, however, very rare instances in which her Curse ability can be useless or even counterproductive. A few enemies are completely Immune to Curse, and disabling Warp stops units from being teleported to safety, which is most notable against [[Final Boss Giga-God|Final Boss Giga God]].

Her immunities to [[Wave Attack]]s, Warp, Curse, Weaken and Surges further help her with the threat posed by such abilities, especially in [[Uncanny Legends]], [[Cats of the Cosmos]] and [[The Aku Realms]] where they are prominently active.

Overall, Kasli the Bane is an extremely powerful unit that holds her edge all the way into the endgame and has almost no drawbacks. She works incredibly well by herself and with other units, allowing her to decimate almost every stage in the game with Curse and damage, easily making her one of the best, if not the best, uber in the game.

